{title: I Will Not Let You Go}
{subtitle: Genesis 32:22–32}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I'll send my wives and children
I sent the gift on ahead of me, every flock and herd
Then I was left alone there on the river bank that night
A man came out of the darkness and he wrestled me till light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will not let you go unless you bless me
Wrestled all night long until the day was breaking
You [C]touched my hip and wrenched it but I'm holding [Gm]on
I will not let you go unless you bless me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He asked me what's your name, I said [C]Jacob is my name
The heel-grab-[Gm]ber, the schemer, the man who carried shame
Your name will no longer be Jacob, but Israel
You have struggled with God and with men that have prevailed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will not let you go unless you bless me
Wrestled all night long until the day was breaking
You touched my hip and wrenched it but I'm holding on
I will not let you [C]go unless you bless me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I named that place [Gm]Peniel
I have seen God face to face
And yet my life was spared
The sun rose a[C]bove him as he passed Penuel
[Gm]And he was limping because of his hip
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Limping in the sunrise
Blessed and holding on
I will not let you go
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
